    "summary": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud praised citizens in Galmudug and Hirshabelle for participating peacefully in parliamentary and local council elections.",
    "content": "Somali President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud on Tuesday commended voters in the federal member states of Galmudug and Hirshabelle for taking part in elections for their regional parliaments and local councils. In a statement, the president described the voting as a significant step in Somalia's democratic development.\n\nThe elections took place across several regions, including Mudug, Galguduud, Hiiraan, and Middle Shabelle. According to the president's office, citizens cast their ballots in a peaceful atmosphere, marking another milestone in the country's gradual transition toward universal suffrage.\n\nPresident Hassan Sheikh specifically applauded the thousands of citizens who exercised their constitutional right to vote. He noted that their participation reflects a growing commitment to shaping Somalia's political future through democratic means.\n\nThis round of elections follows years of indirect voting in Somalia, where clan delegates selected lawmakers. The current government has prioritized direct elections as part of its broader state-building agenda, aiming to strengthen legitimacy and accountability at both federal and regional levels.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these elections carry particular importance. Many diaspora members maintain close ties to Galmudug and Hirshabelle and have supported political processes in their home regions through remittances, advocacy, and occasional return visits. The peaceful conduct of the polls may encourage greater diaspora engagement and investment in local governance.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/30/madaxweyne-xasan-sheekh-oo-bogaadiyey-shacabka-ka-qeyb-galay-doorashooyinka-galmudug-iyo-hirshabeelle/",
