    "content": "Cali Guudlaawe, a candidate for the leadership of Hirshabelle State, has called on the public to participate actively in the elections taking place in Jowhar and other parts of the region. He encouraged residents to go to polling stations and fulfill their civic duty by voting peacefully in the ongoing electoral process.\n\nGuudlaawe also appealed to the community to maintain calm and security during the voting period, and to take part in the elections responsibly. His remarks come as voting is underway in several areas of Hirshabelle.\n\nThe elections in Hirshabelle are part of the broader process to select the region's leadership. Cali Guudlaawe is among the contenders seeking the presidency of the state. The vote in Jowhar and other locations marks a key phase in the indirect electoral process.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the stability and outcome of elections in Hirshabelle carry significant weight. Many diaspora members have family ties to the region and contribute to its economy through remittances. A peaceful and credible electoral process is seen as essential for maintaining stability and fostering development in the state.\n\nDiaspora communities often follow such elections closely, as the results can affect local governance, security, and the political landscape that impacts their relatives and investments back home. The call for peaceful participation aligns with long-standing appeals from international partners for inclusive and non-violent elections in Somalia.\n\nAs voting continues, the focus remains on ensuring a smooth and transparent process. The outcome will shape Hirshabelle's leadership at a time when regional states play a critical role in Somalia's federal system.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/30/madaxweyne-cali-guudlaawe-oo-shacabka-ugu-baaqay-inay-si-weyn-uga-qeyb-qaataan-doorashada/",
